WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
- Have you ever worked in a bar?

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.006
I have.

00:00:04.006 --> 00:00:06.160
- I have. I have.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.340
I feel like every
honestly successful woman

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.870
has at some point.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.040
I started, and it was
funny cause I was like,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.290
when I was in college in England,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.110
I worked in a pub, and so I thought,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.000
oh, this qualifies me
for working in a bar.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.930
I'm a bartender, basically.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.320
So pubs in England, you
do not have the same,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.070
like, demands and you can
pour like a pint of Guinness.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.910
But then I moved to LA.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.290
I went to this place that
was on the Sunset Strip,

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.150
and I said, oh, I'm here to
apply for this job bartending.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.460
And we're like, okay, cool.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.760
So why don't you come in in
two days and just, you know,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.067
make a bunch of your favorite cocktails?

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.163
Like, right.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.320
So I go home. I'm living
with roommates at the time.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.029
I've never made a cocktail in my life.

00:00:51.029 --> 00:00:52.610
I'm living with roommates at the time

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.750
and I go and buy "Bartending for Dummies."

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.780
And I literally think
that somehow in 48 hours,

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.680
I'm going to learn how to be Tom Cruise.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.577
Like, I just think that's
just what's gonna happen.

00:01:03.577 --> 00:01:04.410
- That's awesome.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.070
- So I'm like, okay, a Manhattan,

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.240
or I just try to pick the
simplest cocktail I can,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.073
practice on my roommates,

00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:10.742
and everybody just sort
of humors me with like,

00:01:10.742 --> 00:01:12.110
okay, yeah, this is great.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.170
And so I go back to this place.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.122
It was actually BOA Steakhouse
on Sunset, on Sunset Strip,

00:01:18.122 --> 00:01:20.540
but it has, like, a bar section.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.670
And I make this drink and it's god awful.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.860
And I'm literally, like, measuring it out,

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.943
trying to look really cool
and smooth and like shaking.

00:01:29.134 --> 00:01:30.550
And then at the end of
it, he's like, cool.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.593
So, waitressing.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:37.280
- So you're going to take
the drinks to the tables.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.113
Awesome.

00:01:38.113 --> 00:01:39.050
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.160
- Were you a better waitress?

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.150
- I mean, I made up for in
enthusiasm what I lacked

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.090
in punctuality, I would say.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.360
I was like, my favorite...

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.490
I worked... I actually have
so many choice experiences

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.827
from the Cat and Fiddle
all in my run-up to -

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:55.720
- Oh, the Cat and Fiddle.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.530
- Booking my first acting gigs.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.600
I know, it's not there
anymore, but it was on Sunset

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.540
and so much fun.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.620
And it was like, I
think one of the nights,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.080
it was like, it was pre Oscar night,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.150
and Adrien Brody was at a table

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.730
with a bunch of really amazing people.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.070
And they all ordered Hendricks, Hennessy,

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.130
something that was expensive.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:16.963
I don't know.

00:02:16.963 --> 00:02:18.400
And simple by the way.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.870
And it took me so long to bring it

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.107
that by the time I brought
probably the wrong drinks,

00:02:22.107 --> 00:02:23.540
they had all left

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.830
because they had to be
somewhere, obviously the Oscars.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.810
And they, but left me
a hundred dollar tip,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.090
and I had never even brought
their drinks for them.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.270
So I'm like, okay.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.300
So I owe Adrien Brody a
shot or a hundred bucks.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.550
- Either way, either way.

